== touch advances the modification time of an existing file:
advanced
== touch -c still does not create a missing file:
ghost-missing
== touch -r copies both timestamps:
copied
== touch -a updates the access time and keeps the modification time:
updated
== touch -m updates the modification time and keeps the access time:
updated
== touch -t sets the requested timestamp:
set
== touch -t accepts an eight-digit timestamp:
set
== touch -t accepts a ten-digit timestamp:
set
